    <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
            <p class="sec-sub">Real questions Chennai logistics + courier + freight operators ask us.</p>
            <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;">
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How does Chennai differ from Mumbai for freight forwarding marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Chennai is auto + component + engineering-goods export dominant vs Mumbai's FMCG + apparel + D2C dominance. Chennai buyers are OEM + component-manufacturer supply-chain heads; Mumbai buyers are D2C brand ops + apparel export houses. Marketing content, ABM TALs, and trade publication choices differ materially.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Should we produce Tamil-language creative for Chennai marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes for local courier + South India 3PL. Tamil creative on Meta + Google outperforms English-only by 25-40% on cost + engagement for local + Tamil Nadu regional catchment. Not needed for enterprise B2B freight forwarding (English-only) or MAA international freight (English + occasionally Hindi).</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is the biggest freight forwarding opportunity from Chennai?</h3><div class="faq-a">Auto Ro-Ro exports to GCC + Middle East (large-volume + high-value, growing India-to-Africa opportunity), plus specialised electronics + pharma air-cargo. Chennai + Ennore + Kattupalli Ro-Ro capacity + Sriperumbudur auto manufacturing base = distinct category leadership opportunity for specialist auto freight forwarders.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How does Chennai's NRI + GCC diaspora affect courier marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Chennai has one of India's largest GCC-diaspora populations (Kuwait, Bahrain, UAE, Saudi). International courier + document + parcel services to GCC destinations see significant repeat + word-of-mouth demand. Marketing content on India-to-GCC service tiers + rates + timelines converts well.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Should Chennai 3PL operators target Tamil Nadu D2C brands specifically?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes as a distinct segment. Chennai + South India D2C ecosystem is emerging (smaller than Mumbai / Bengaluru but growing). Tamil Nadu + Kerala + Andhra + South Karnataka distribution catchment is a natural Chennai 3PL advantage. Segment-specific case studies + integration marketing on Unicommerce + Vinculum + regional platforms.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is a realistic marketing budget for a Chennai-based auto freight forwarder?</h3><div class="faq-a">Rs 3-8 lakh / month for mid-market (Rs 25-200 Cr rev). Heavy on LinkedIn ABM (auto OEM + Tier 1/2 supplier decision-makers), route-specific SEO (India-to-GCC + India-to-Africa + India-to-LATAM), trade PR (ACMA + Auto Component publications), and speaker slots at auto + freight industry events.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Are there specific Chennai regulations to market compliance around?</h3><div class="faq-a">Chennai Port Trust + Ennore + Kattupalli port procedures, Tamil Nadu GST + e-invoicing, CTA (Chennai Metropolitan) transport permits, TNPCB pollution + cold-chain compliance. Auto-specific: export benefit schemes (RoDTEP, DBK), auto-component HSN classification. Compliance content targeted at these ranks well because Tamil Nadu-specific.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How do Chennai couriers handle T Nagar + Anna Nagar traffic + delivery windows?</h3><div class="faq-a">Chennai has moderately restrictive HGV timing (typically 7 am - 10 pm restricted on inner-city routes with variations by area). T Nagar + Anna Nagar + Adyar delivery-window navigation is a competitive differentiator for local couriers. Ops planning shifts to non-restricted windows + last-mile 2-wheeler + 3-wheeler fleet. Marketing narratives around "guaranteed delivery within Chennai traffic constraints" resonate strongly.</div></div>
